<section_role>
PROBLEM

Goal:
- Make the problem feel real, costly, and explainable.
- Show why the reader’s current attempts fail or backfire.
- Build urgency through consequences, not pressure.

Execution rules:
- Assume the reader has already tried common approaches and feels stuck.
- Describe the lived experience clearly and concretely (how it feels, how it disrupts routine).
- Call out the common failure pattern (switching products, relying on rich textures, chasing “stronger” fixes) without judgment.
- Explain the underlying cause at a practical level — why this keeps happening.
- Raise stakes using realistic costs: discomfort, irritation, wasted money/time, inconsistency, sensitivity flares, breakouts, pilling.
- Do NOT introduce solutions, advice, or “what to do next”.
- Do NOT mention products, brands, or ingredients framed as fixes.

Banned patterns:
- Generic category framing (“Common problems with…”, “Many people struggle with…”).
- Checklist or listicle voice.
- Vague claims without a concrete cause (“because it doesn’t work”).
- Transitional solution language (“this is why you need…”, “the answer is…”).

Formatting & structure:
- If section.heading exists, start with `## {{section.heading}}`.
- Do NOT force a specific number of paragraphs.
- Let the explanation unfold naturally, ending with a clear sense of *why the problem persists*.
</section_role>
